"electrical waste, the average amount of e-waste that one UK individual "
"creates in a lifetime. (Photograph by James T.M. Towill and [published]"
"(https://www.geograph.org.uk/photo/2637892) under a [CC-BY-SA-2.0](https://"
"spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-2.0.html) license.)](images/sec1_geograph-2637892-"
"by-James-T-M-Towill_1600x1200.jpg)"
msgstr ""
"![Imatge de l'estàtua «WEEE Man», que està feta de 3,3 tones mètriques de "
"residus electrònics, la quantitat mitjana de residus electrònics que una "
"persona del Regne Unit crea en tota la vida. (Fotografiada per James T.M. "
"Towill i [publicada](https://www.geograph.org.uk/photo/2637892) segons una "
"llicència [CC-BY-SA-2.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-2.0.html)]"
"(images/sec1_geograph-2637892-by-James-T-M-Towill_1600x1200.jpg)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:111
msgid ""
"E-waste is [considered](https://www.weforum.org/reports/a-new-circular-"
"vision-for-electronics-time-for-a-global-reboot/) the “fastest-growing waste "
"stream in the world”, with 44.7 million metric tons generated in 2016&mdash;"
"equivalent to [4,500 Eiffel Towers](https://www.itu.int/en/ITU-D/Climate-"
"Change/Documents/GEM%202017/Global-E-waste%20Monitor%202017%20.pdf), which, "
"when stacked, is 17 times higher than Mount Everest. In 2018, an estimated "
"50 million metric tons of e-waste was reported, motivating the UN to refer "
"to a “[tsunami of e-waste](https://news.un.org/en/story/2015/05/497772) "
"rolling out over the world”. The numbers continue to rise: in 2021, an "
"estimated [57 million metric tons](https://www.bbc.com/news/science-"
"environment-61350996) of e-waste was generated globally. [Less than 20 "
"percent](https://weee-forum.org/ws_news/international-e-waste-day-2021/) of "
"it is collected and recycled, and although it makes up [only 2%](https://www."
"forbes.com/sites/vianneyvaute/2019/04/23/with-love-from-an-oregon-prison-how-"
"eric-lundgren-is-going-to-help-you-recycle-all-your-electronics/) of trash "
"in landfills, it contributes to almost 70% of the toxic waste found there."
msgstr ""
"Els residus electrònics es [consideren](https://www.weforum.org/reports/a-"
"new-circular-vision-for-electronics-time-for-a-global-reboot/) el «flux de "
"residus de creixement més ràpid al món», amb 44,7 milions de tones mètriques "
"generades el 2016, equivalent a [4,500 Torres Eiffel](https://www.itu.int/en/"
"ITU-D/Climate-Change/Documents/GEM%202017/Global-E-waste%20Monitor%202017%20."
"pdf), que quan s'apilen, són 17 vegades més altes que l'Everest. El 2018, es "
"va informar d'una estimació de 50 milions de tones mètriques de residus "
"electrònics, motivant a l'ONU a referir-se a un «[tsunami de residus "
"electrònics](https://news.un.org/en/story/2015/05/497772) que s'estén per "
"tot el món». Les xifres continuen augmentant: el 2021, s'estima que es van "
"generar [57 milions de tones mètriques](https://www.bbc.com/news/science-"
"environment-61350996) a nivell mundial. [Menys del 20 per cent](https://weee-"
"forum.org/ws_news/international-e-waste-day-2021/) es recupera i recicla, i "
"encara que constitueix [només el 2%](https://www.forbes.com/sites/"
"vianneyvaute/2019/04/23/with-love-from-an-oregon-prison-how-eric-lundgren-is-"
"going-to-help-you-recycle-all-your-electronics/) d'escombraries en els "
"abocadors, contribueixen a gairebé el 70% dels residus tòxics trobats allí."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:113
msgid ""
